==Dutch==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Nl-boer.ogg|audio}}

===Etymology 1===
Germanic, from an eastern dialect (perhaps [[West Frisian]], like its cognates {{term|gebuur|lang=nl}}) buur 'neighbor', Old English {{term|gebur|ġebūr|lang=ang}} etc. ultimately derived from [[bûr]] 'habitation'

====Noun====
{{nl-noun|g=m|boeren|boertje}}

# A [[farmer]], [[peasant]]
# '''-boer''' (''in compounds'') [[merchant]] (and sometimes producer) of a certain product group, mainly foods, often named after it, e.g. [[melkboer]] 'milkman'
# A [[boor]], [[yokel]], [[ruffian]]
# {{slang|lang=nl}} A [[jack]] (playing cards)

=====Synonyms=====
